nt address: Department of Electronics, Weizmann Institute of Science, Rehovot, Israel.\nL82: \nL83: 【18†PDF】\nL84: \nL85: Phys. Rev. Lett. 53, 311 – Published 23 July, 1984\nL86: DOI: https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.53.311\nL87: \nL88: [Button: Export Citation]\nL89: \nL90: Show metrics\nL91: ## Abstract\nL92: \nL93: Time development of cellular automata in $d$ dimensions is mapped onto equilibrium statistical mechanics of Ising models in $d+1\\mathrm{}$ dimensions. Directed percolation is equivalent to a cellular automaton, and thus to an Ising model. For a particular case of directed percolation we find ${\\nu }_{\\parallel }=2\\mathrm{}$, ${\\nu }_{\\perp }=1\\mathrm{}$, ${\\eta }_{\\perp }=0\\mathrm{}$.\nL94: \nL95: [Button: Close]\nL96: \nL97: [Button: Prev][Button: Next]\nL98: \nL99: ##\nL100: \nL101: 【19†View figure in article】\nL102: # Authorization Required\nL103: \nL104: We need you to provide your credentials before accessing this content.\nL105: \nL106: ## Log in via your institution\nL107: \nL108: If your institution provides access using Shibboleth/OpenAthens log in.\nL109: \nL110: ## Log in via APS Member Subscription\nL111: \nL112: If you have a personal subscription through your APS membership please log in.\nL113: \nL114: Starting August 1, 2019 APS member subscribers will need to log in using your member credentials instead of your APS Journal Account.\nL115: \nL116: 【20†APS Member Log In】\nL117: ## Other Options\nL118: \nL119:   * 【21†Buy Article »】\nL120:   * 【22†Log in with APS Journals Account】\nL121:   * 【23†Log in with username/password provided by your institution】\nL122:   * 【24†Get access through a U.S. public or high school】\nL123: ## 【18†References (Subscription Required)】\nL124: \nL125: [Button: Outline][Button: Information]\nL126: \nL127:   * 【25†Citing Articles (442)】\nL128:   * 【26†Abstract】\nL129:   * 【27†References】\nL130: \nL131: Phys. Rev. Lett. 53, 311– Published 23 July, 1984\nL132: \nL133: 【28†Vol. 53, Iss. 4 — 23 July 19