re model\nL73: \nL74: 【16†B. Drossel】 and 【17†F. Schwabl】\nL75: \nL76:   * ^{}Physik-Department der Technischen Universität München, D-8046 Garching, Germany\nL77: \nL78: 【18†PDF】\nL79: \nL80: Phys. Rev. Lett. 69, 1629 – Published 14 September, 1992\nL81: \nL82: DOI: https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.1629\nL83: \nL84: [Button: Export Citation]\nL85: \nL86: Show metrics\nL87: ## Abstract\nL88: A forest-fire model is introduced which contains a lightning probability f. This leads to a self-organized critical state in the limit f→0 provided that the time scales of tree growth and burning down of forest clusters are separated. We derive scaling laws and calculate all critical exponents. The values of the critical exponents are confirmed by computer simulations.\nL89: For a two-dimensional system, we show that the forest density in the critical state assumes its minimum possible value, i.e., that energy dissipation is maximum.\nL90: [Button: Close]\nL91: \nL92: [Button: Prev][Button: Next]\nL93: ##\nL94: \nL95: 【19†View figure in article】\nL96: \nL97: # Authorization Required\nL98: \nL99: We need you to provide your credentials before accessing this content.\nL100: \nL101: ## Log in via your institution\nL102: \nL103: If your institution provides access using Shibboleth/OpenAthens log in.\nL104: ## Log in via APS Member Subscription\nL105: \nL106: If you have a personal subscription through your APS membership please log in.\nL107: \nL108: Starting August 1, 2019 APS member subscribers will need to log in using your member credentials instead of your APS Journal Account.\nL109: \nL110: 【20†APS Member Log In】\nL111: \nL112: ## Other Options\nL113: \nL114:   * 【21†Buy Article »】\nL115:   * 【22†Log in with APS Journals Account】\nL116:   * 【23†Log in with username/password provided by your institution】\nL117:   * 【24†Get access through a U.S. public or high school】\nL118: ## 【18†References (Subscription Required)】\nL119: \nL120: [Button: Outline][Button: Information]\nL